{% doc %}
  Sizes a hero or page-header title to its box, so the longest word fits on a phone
  (DESIGN.md §4.3).

  Outputs a style attribute that sets --gs-fit-chars to the length of the title's longest word.
  gs-components.css sizes the title as 100% of its box divided by (letters x 0.74em), capped at
  the H1 or display size. Without it the CSS assumes 12 letters (CONVERSATION).

  @param {string} text - The title

  @example
  <h1 class="gs-h1"{% render 'gs-fit', text: page.title %}>{{ page.title | escape }}</h1>
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign longest = 1
  assign words = text | strip_html | strip | split: ' '
  for word in words
    assign n = word | size
    if n > longest
      assign longest = n
    endif
  endfor
  echo ' style="--gs-fit-chars: ' | append: longest | append: '"'
-%}
